{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>לעברך.</b> That you pass into the covenant. And it is not tenable to expound it as לְהַעֲבִירְךָ, but rather like לַעֲשֹׂתְכֶם אֹתָם." "<b>לעברך בברית.</b> The way of 'passing' is thus: those who cut covenants would make a partition on one side and a partition on the other side, and pass between them, as it is said: ״הָעֵגֶל אֲשֶׁר כָּרְתוּ לִשְׁנַיִם וַיַּעַבְרוּ בֵּין בְּתָרָיו״ (Jeremiah 34)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:49.852204615Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}